# LeakSanitizer suppressions for tools/m2_harness.sh (docs/m2-r3-closeout-headers.md "quit").
#
# Until M2-R3 no harness run reached a normal exit: every quit stopped at GoK's munmap(heap, 0) assertion first. With
# that fixed, LeakSanitizer runs at exit and reports these allocations that nothing frees before exit(). None is a
# Cataclysm delta and none grows during a run (each is made once at start-up). Every other leak still fails the run.
#
# Third-party libraries (not this tree's code):
leak:libdbus-1.so
# OpenGL driver state made inside SDL_GL_CreateContext (render.c setupPixelFormat); the driver frees it at unload
leak:setupPixelFormat
#
# GoK start-up allocations never released at quit (owner: stage 5 networking / stage 3 render init, which port these
# start-up and shut-down paths):
# - SDL mutexes made by mgStartup (MultiplayerGame.c) and titanGameStartup (TitanNet.c); titanGameShutdown, which
#   destroys two of them, is never called on the quit path
leak:mgStartup
leak:titanGameStartup
# - a display-mode record made by rinEnumeratePrimary (rinit.c) during InitWindow
leak:rinEnumeratePrimary
